    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-184639",
      "knowledge_point_id": "957a2f61-61b1-5675-ba84-5348a47af986",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding Unions and Intersections of Finite Families of Indexed Sets",
      "problem": "Find ${⋃}_{i=0}^{2}{X}_{i}$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{X}_{0}={-2,-1,2},\\,{X}_{1}={-1,0,2},\\,{X}_{2}={-2,0,3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The union of a family of indexed sets is the set containing all elements belonging to *at least one* set in the indexed family:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nThe notation ${⋃}_{i=0}^{2}$ means that our index set is \n${0,1,2}.$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋃}_{i=0}^{2}{X}_{i} & ={X}_{0}\\cup {X}_{1}\\cup {X}_{2} \\\\  & ={-2,-1,2}\\,\\cup \\,{-1,0,2}\\,\\cup \\,{-2,0,3} \\\\  & ={-2,-1,0,2,3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{-2,-1,2,3}"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{-2,0,2,3}"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{-3,-2,-1,0,2,3}"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "∅"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{-2,-1,0,2,3}"
            }
          ],
          "correct_value": "{-2,-1,0,2,3}",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "correct_origin": "ma_successful_grade"
