    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-174432",
      "knowledge_point_id": "957a2f61-61b1-5675-ba84-5348a47af986",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding Unions and Intersections of Finite Families of Indexed Sets",
      "problem": "Find ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}$, given that $I={-2,1,2},$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{X}_{-2}={-2,-1,0},\\,{X}_{1}={0,1},\\,{X}_{2}={0,1,2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The union of a family of indexed sets is the set containing all elements belonging to *at least one* set in the indexed family:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nTherefore, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i} & ={X}_{-2}\\cup {X}_{1}\\cup {X}_{2} \\\\  & ={-2,-1,0}\\,\\cup \\,{0,1}\\,\\cup \\,{0,1,2} \\\\  & ={-2,-1,0,1,2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
